{"id":28704,"slug":"female-trouble","title":"Female Trouble","year":1974,"country":"United States","duration":97,"spine":929,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28704-female-trouble","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/158358e5a3c887eb8da3f2fd7c88ca32/M2SseBDqHqhbAX1r730ezWGJFjcTxE_large.jpg","description":"Glamour has never been more grotesque than in Female Trouble, which injects the Hollywood melodrama with anarchic decadence. Divine, director John Waters’ larger-than-life muse, engulfs the screen with charisma as Dawn Davenport, the living embodiment of the film’s lurid mantra, “Crime is beauty,” who progresses from a teenage nightmare hell-bent on getting cha-cha heels for Christmas to a fame monster whose egomaniacal impulses land her in the electric chair. Shot in Waters’ native Baltimore on 16 mm, with a cast drawn from his beloved troupe of regulars, the Dreamlanders (including Mink Stole, David Lochary, Mary Vivian Pearce, Edith Massey, and Cookie Mueller), this film­—the director’s favorite of his work with Divine—comes to life through the tinsel-toned vision of production designer Vincent Peranio and costume designer/makeup artist Van Smith. An endlessly quotable fan favorite, Female Trouble offers up perverse pleasures that never fail to satisfy.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"John Waters","slug":"john-waters"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Divine","role":"Dawn Davenport/Earl Peterson","slug":"divine"},{"actor":"David Lochary","role":"Donald Dasher","slug":"david-lochary"},{"actor":"Mary Vivian Pearce","role":"Donna Dasher","slug":"mary-vivian-pearce"},{"actor":"Mink Stole","role":"Taffy Davenport","slug":"mink-stole"},{"actor":"Edith Massey","role":"Aunt Ida","slug":"edith-massey"},{"actor":"Cookie Mueller","role":"Concetta","slug":"cookie-mueller"},{"actor":"Susan Walsh","role":"Chicklette","slug":"susan-walsh"},{"actor":"Michael Potter","role":"Gater","slug":"michael-potter"},{"actor":"Ed Peranio","role":"Wink","slug":